# CODEOWNERS for the Trivy ignore surface.
#
# Replace @ctfjake with your @org/security-team; this auto-requests their review
# on any pull request that adds or changes a Trivy ignore (enforce with branch
# protection requiring CODEOWNERS review).
#
# Every path below is a place a security finding can be suppressed: the
# .trivyignore files that waive findings globally, and intended-public/ where
# reasoned inline #trivy:ignore comments live. Owning these paths means a
# security reviewer is pulled onto any pull request that touches a waiver.

# Global and example Trivy ignore files at the repo root.
/.trivyignore         @ctfjake
/.trivyignore.*       @ctfjake
.trivyignore.example  @ctfjake

# Any .trivyignore file anywhere in the tree.
**/.trivyignore       @ctfjake
**/.trivyignore.*     @ctfjake

# The intended-public example, where inline #trivy:ignore waivers live.
/intended-public/     @ctfjake
